# Brief: Click Ten

Objective (quoted): "Make "Click Ten" as a tiny web game played in the browser: one page with a button and a counter; each click adds one, and at ten clicks the game shows "You did it!" and a button to play again, which resets the counter to zero. One HTML file with its script and style inside it; no images, sound or libraries."

Focus: a single `index.html` (inline CSS/JS), no external assets. Counter starts 0; each click +1; at 10 show "You did it!" and a play-again button; play again resets to 0 and restores the game. No further clicks past 10.

Acceptance: I load the file in a headless browser, click 10 times, see the message, click play again, see 0.
Not established: file name (assumed `index.html` at game-developer repo root).
